# Geoscience Australia "DEM of Australia derived from LiDAR 5 Metre Grid", Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 (© Commonwealth of
# Australia, Geoscience Australia). Bare-earth heights from LiDAR surveys 2001 to 2015, so coverage follows the surveys and is not
# complete. Catalogue record: https://ecat.ga.gov.au/geonetwork/srv/api/records/22be4b55-2465-4320-e053-10a3070a5236
# If the service address stops working, copy the current WCS address from that record.
DEM_WCS_URL="${DEM_WCS_URL:-https://services.ga.gov.au/gis/services/DEM_LiDAR_5m_2025/MapServer/WCSServer}"
# Set when the service offers more than one coverage (the download script lists them). The service has one, named 1.
DEM_COVERAGE="${DEM_COVERAGE:-}"
# The service answers in degrees only (EPSG:4326 or GDA94 geographic, EPSG:4283). Files are kept as they arrive in GDA94.
DEM_REQUEST_SRID="${DEM_REQUEST_SRID:-4283}"
# Each request covers a square of this many degrees (about 4.7 by 5.5 km), kept small so the service never refuses it.
DEM_CELL_DEG="${DEM_CELL_DEG:-0.05}"
# The service's own pixel size in degrees (from its coverage description); requests ask for that resolution.
DEM_PIXEL_DEG_X="${DEM_PIXEL_DEG_X:-0.000055063478}"
DEM_PIXEL_DEG_Y="${DEM_PIXEL_DEG_Y:-0.000051601233}"
# Slope needs metres, so the loader reprojects to GDA94 / MGA zone 56 at this pixel size. The cadastre is GDA2020; the 1.8 m
# difference is well inside a 5 m pixel.
DEM_SRID="${DEM_SRID:-28356}"
DEM_PIXEL_M="${DEM_PIXEL_M:-5}"
# Heights outside this range are treated as no data (the service's fill value is far below it).
DEM_MIN_M="${DEM_MIN_M:--50}"
DEM_MAX_M="${DEM_MAX_M:-1500}"
DEM_TILE_PX="${DEM_TILE_PX:-256}"
